                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef7edbd0-041f-338d-b2d4-ab32fa036b56",
                        "entry_id": "f4d6c8b7-ec41-3cfe-8429-b276c0e0ca2c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dance derived from the twist, popular in the 1960s."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35e34937-cebc-4428-9783-adcea7a6c5be",
                                "sense_id": "ef7edbd0-041f-338d-b2d4-ab32fa036b56",
                                "text": "She [...] loves to cook, sew and dance. She's up on all the latest steps like the frug, the hully-gully and the surf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62cd4cd0-bbc1-44d9-a539-2d645140fffc",
                                "sense_id": "ef7edbd0-041f-338d-b2d4-ab32fa036b56",
                                "text": "The snake did the frug, the monkey did the shake. The crowd, mostly young couples, tourists and kids, loved it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ffa17de3-b999-47b4-800d-bb195f13f73b",
                                "sense_id": "ef7edbd0-041f-338d-b2d4-ab32fa036b56",
                                "text": "They were doing a modified frug, a dance Ruth had learned—and abandoned—in high school."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46485057-4d6d-4fc4-8380-581e0ac7658f",
                                "sense_id": "ef7edbd0-041f-338d-b2d4-ab32fa036b56",
                                "text": "In telegraphic succession, the parents two-step, Charleston, lindy, twist, and frug, their dance harmony always splintered apart by their offspring."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
